## CRITICAL EXECUTION PROTOCOL

Before deciding HOW to solve any task, you MUST first discover the available built-in tools in folder: interpreter

Your implementation plan is NOT allowed to be created until tool discovery has finished.

Workflow:

1. Inspect the interpreter directory.
2. Read the documentation comments inside the available tool files.
3. Determine whether a built-in tool already supports the requested task.
4. If a suitable tool exists, you MUST use it.
5. Only if no suitable tool exists, or it fails after execution, may you plan an external solution.

Planning an external implementation before tool discovery is considered an incorrect workflow.